      "description": "Show the local task queue: every task in brief, or one task in full. Use when: the user asks what is queued, whether a task finished, or for its result. Do not use to change a task (use cancel_task, update_deadline or retry_task) or to set result delivery (use set_delivery). Behavior: no network or login; marks a completed or failed task read when shown, nothing else; never changes a status. Returns: without task_id, total, last_tick_at and tasks (task_id, title, status, region, scheduled_for); with task_id, its record with prompt, result, receipt and delivery. Throws on an unknown task_id.",
