      "description": "Cancel one queued or scheduled task by task_id; to cancel every pending task use cancel_all. Use when: the user drops one task. Do not use to run it later (use update_deadline) or to rerun a failed task (use retry_task). Behavior: marks the task cancelled in the local queue and redacts its stored prompt; no network or login. A finished task comes back unchanged; a repeat call changes nothing. A repeating task skips this occurrence and queues the next; series=true ends the series. Returns: task_id, status, completed_at, plus series_id and series_ended for a series. Throws on an unknown task_id.",
